{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_three_process_split", "label": "Three-process architecture (web / api / ml)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The split exists so the computationally/scientifically hard part (rPPG extraction) can be developed, tested, and iterated on entirely independently of the web application shell."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_zero_infra_mode", "label": "Zero-infra local mode (SQLite + in-process queue)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SQLite plus an in-process job queue means no Docker, Postgres or Redis is required to run the full stack locally."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_apps_web", "label": "apps/web React SPA", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contains zero signal-processing logic; it only ever displays what the API returns."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_apps_api", "label": "apps/api Express service", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Owns video storage bookkeeping, the analysis queue, the SQLite schema and WebSocket progress events, but contains zero OpenCV/ML code - its only contact with the science is a single HTTP client (python.service.ts)."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_services_ml", "label": "services/ml FastAPI ML service", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stateless: given a video path and parameters it returns structured JSON, owning 100% of video processing, rPPG extraction, feature engineering and cue fusion, and knows nothing about SQLite or HTTP sessions."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_request_flow", "label": "Video upload to result request flow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_analysis_queue", "label": "In-process analysis queue (analysis.queue.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Concurrency 2 with retry and exponential backoff (up to 3 retries, 5s backoff) keeps the local stack zero-infra; BullMQ/Redis were removed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_python_service", "label": "python.service.ts ML HTTP client", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_polling_progress", "label": "Polling-based progress reporting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /v1/analyse is a single blocking call, so the Node side polls the ML progress registry every 700ms; this keeps the transport simple (plain HTTP, no SSE/WebSocket fan-in between services) while still driving the per-stage progress bar. ProgressCallback in end_to_end.py is the seam if streaming is ever wanted."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_end_to_end_pipeline", "label": "app/pipeline/end_to_end.py orchestration", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_progress_registry", "label": "app/core/progress.py in-memory progress registry", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_signal_artifacts", "label": "Signal artifact files (storage/signals/{analysis_id}.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_visual_trace_artifacts", "label": "Visualization trace files (storage/visuals/{analysis_id}.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_pipeline_visualization", "label": "Pipeline tab visualization trace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FrameTraceCollector samples a normalised per-frame trace at ~5 Hz bounded to 600 entries and the file is written in a finally block, so even failed analyses show how far they got."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_ws_fanout", "label": "Single-process WebSocket fan-out", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The queue runs in the same process as the HTTP server so emitAnalysisEvent always reaches every connected browser with no cross-process adapter - a deliberate consequence of zero-infra mode; a multi-instance deployment would need socket.io-redis plus an external queue."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_data_storage_decisions", "label": "Data storage decisions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raw video lives on disk never in the database; results are a single JSON-encoded text column because SQLite has no native Json type; large arrays are externalized to artifact files; all storage paths resolve against the repo root by walking up to pnpm-workspace.yaml."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_known_gaps", "label": "Known gaps", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_apps_web", "target": "docs_architecture_apps_api", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_apps_api", "target": "docs_architecture_services_ml", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_apps_api", "target": "docs_architecture_analysis_queue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_analysis_queue", "target": "docs_architecture_python_service", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_python_service", "target": "docs_architecture_progress_registry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_end_to_end_pipeline", "target": "docs_architecture_progress_registry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_services_ml", "target": "docs_a